;
; The cheapest immediate encoding for each 64-bit constant: SETR (sign-
; extended imm32), SETRU (zero-extended, for [2^31, 2^32): MMIO addresses,
; 32-bit masks), SETR64 only for a genuine 64-bit value.  Their short forms
; cover -128..255 (SETRU_SH for 128..255).  The same choice for the immediate
; of an add (ADDI / ADDV / MINUSV), a compare (CMPRV / CMPRVU) and a bitwise
; op (ANDV.. zero-extended / ANDI.. sign-extended, e.g. the `& -8` of an
; alignment round-up).  A non-PIC symbol address is zero-extended (SETRU),
; like the PIC LEAPC.

